From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Abbott <cwabbott0@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:48:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/graphics_state: Don't get IAL state when not needed

When emulating classic renderpasses using dynamic rendering, getting the
input attachment location state involves querying the emulated render
pass. If there is only vertex input state, then the render pass must be
ignored, but the common code was still querying the render pass, even
though it never actually used it. We did later update the spec to say
that in such a case the render pass must still be NULL or valid, so the
code worked for drivers which never pass in a driver_rp and always use
emulated render passes.  However, in turnip we do not emulate render
passes, and furthermore we try to be efficient and avoid constructing a
driver_rp if unnecessary, as the common code should not need it. If the
user then constructed a vertex input only pipeline but passed a
valid-but-ignored renderPass, the driver_rp would be NULL and the common
code would query the renderPass assuming it's a vk_render_pass, but it
was actually a tu_render_pass, and the common code crashed. Avoid
dereferencing it in this case and just make it NULL.

Fixes: be2532fc003 ("vk/pass: Add input attachment location info")
Reviewed-by: Samuel Pitoiset <samuel.pitoiset@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Boris Brezillon <boris.brezillon@collabora.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4503d6ea4a4fd8a54bb7d8a1b6180571d4737b4e)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45215>
(cherry picked from commit 0eddb8f6bfc8e517d8888b8ee2b1f53b538e349f)
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_graphics_state.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_graphics_state.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_graphics_state.c
index 990c3d5f378..bc7114c99c7 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_graphics_state.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_graphics_state.c
@@ -1819,10 +1819,12 @@ vk_graphics_pipeline_state_fill(const struct vk_device *device,
    const VkPipelineFragmentShadingRateStateCreateInfoKHR *fsr_info =
       vk_find_struct_const(info->pNext, PIPELINE_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_STATE_CREATE_INFO_KHR);
 
-   const VkRenderingInputAttachmentIndexInfoKHR *ial_info =
-      !driver_rp ? vk_get_pipeline_rendering_ial_info(info)
-                 : vk_find_struct_const(
-                      info->pNext, RENDERING_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_INDEX_INFO_KHR);
+   const VkRenderingInputAttachmentIndexInfoKHR *ial_info = NULL;
+   if (needs & MESA_VK_GRAPHICS_STATE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_MAP_BIT) {
+      ial_info = !driver_rp ? vk_get_pipeline_rendering_ial_info(info)
+                            : vk_find_struct_const(
+                                info->pNext, RENDERING_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_INDEX_INFO_KHR);
+   }
 
    const VkRenderingAttachmentLocationInfoKHR *cal_info =
       vk_find_struct_const(info->pNext, RENDERING_ATTACHMENT_LOCATION_INFO_KHR);
